    "headline": "some beneficial rain on saturday; big heatwave next week?",
    "dateLine": "1:00 p.m. Friday, June 26, 2026, Update",
    "excerpt": "As expected, a weak cold front sagged through the Commonwealth on Thursday night and brought some early-morning showers to south-central and southeastern PA. Areas south of the Mason-Dixon Line received little if any measurable rain, and less than 0.25\" fell across most of the Lower Susquehanna Valley with a measly 0.06\" at Millersville University. Only northern Perry and northern Dauphin Counties received 0.50-1.00\" of rain from thunderstorms late Thursday evening. …",
